 <button class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary\" onclick=\"getSession()\">\n+                                    <i class=\"ph-fill ph-key\"></i>\n+                                    <span>تجديد جلسة المتصفح (Get Session)</span>\n+                                    <span id=\"session-status\" class=\"status-icon\"></span>\n+                                </button>\n+                            </div>\n+                        </div>\n+                    </div>\n+                </div>\n+            </div>\n+\n+        </main>\n     </div>\n \n+    <!-- The original screen-home is removed. We use screen-new as the home page. \n+         To keep app.js happy if it references screen-home, we add a dummy hidden div -->\n+    <div id=\"screen-home\" style=\"display:none;\"></div>\n+\n     <script src=\"../static/app.js\"></script>\n+    <script>\n+        // Override showScreen to handle active states on sidebar\n+        const originalShowScreen = window.showScreen;\n+        window.showScreen = function(screenId, element = null) {\n+            // Call original if it exists\n+            if (typeof originalShowScreen === 'function') {\n+                originalShowScreen(screenId);\n+            } else {\n+                document.querySelectorAll('.screen').forEach(s => s.classList.remove('active'));\n+                const target = document.getElementById(screenId);\n+                if (target) target.classList.add('active');\n+            }\n+            \n+            // Update sidebar active class\n+            if (element) {\n+                document.querySelectorAll('.nav-item').forEach(btn => btn.classList.remove('active'));\n+                element.classList.add('active');\n+            }\n+        };\n+        // Auto select first nav item\n+        document.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", () => {\n+            const firstNav = document.querySelector('.nav-item');\n+            if (firstNav) firstNav.classList.add('active');\n+        });\n+    </script>\n </body>\n </html>\n \n[diff_block_end]\n\nPlease note that the above snippet only shows the MODIFIED lines from the last change. It shows up to 3 lines of unchanged lines before and after the modified lines. The actual file contents may have many more lines not shown."}
