ent.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n**Current Status:** I just pushed a massive rewrite of the HTML and CSS to give the app a highly professional, native desktop feel in response to the user's harsh critique of the previous UI.\n\n**Immediate Next Steps for the Next Agent:**\n1. Do absolutely nothing until the user responds. They are currently testing the new UI.\n2. If the user reports UI bugs, JS errors, or layout issues (e.g., buttons not working due to ID changes in the HTML rewrite), read `desktop_app/static/app.js` to ensure the JS logic aligns perfectly with the new `index.html` IDs.\n3. Once the UI is approved, the final step is End-to-End Testing: The user needs to run a full pipeline (select PDF shortages + JSON warehouses -> Submit -> Review Excel -> Apply Reviews) to confirm the app behaves exactly like the CLI did.\n\nYou have the 7 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.agents/agents/desktop-builder/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:17:02Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.agents/agents/pharmacy-builder/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T10:46:04Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790006220414]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790006220414.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T15:57:26Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790006245677]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790006245677.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T15:57:26Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790008142552]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790008142552.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T16:29:03Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: implementation_plan]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/implementation_plan.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:08:05Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: task]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/task.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:24:15Z\n\n# Subagents\nThe following subagents were spawned during this conversation (up to 20).\nView the conversation log to see the full conversation with the subagent and use send_message with the conversation_id to communicate with them.\n\n{\n  \"spec\": {\n    \"typeName\": \"pharmacy-builder\",\n    \"role\": \"Project structure builder\",\n    \"initialPrompt\": \"Create the following files for the pharmacy drug matching project at d:\\\\AI_Engineer\\\\Pharmacy-agy:\\n\\n## 1. requirements.txt\\nInclude these dependencies:\\n- openpyxl (Excel reading/writing)\\n- rapidfuzz (fuzzy text matching)\\n- requests (HTTP for Unstructured API)\\n- google-genai (Gemini API - the new SDK, not google-generativeai)\\n- python-dotenv (env file for API keys)\\n\\n## 2. .env.example\\nTemplate with:\\n- UNSTRUCTURED_API_KEY=your_key_here\\n- GEMINI_API_KEY=your_key_here\\n\\n## 3. .gitignore\\nStandard Python gitignore + .env + data/output/ + __pycache__\\n\\n## 4. src/__init__.py (empty)\\n\\n## 5. src/config.py\\nConfiguration module that:\\n- Loads API keys from environment variables (with python-dotenv)\\n- Has a Config dataclass with:\\n  - unstructured_api_key: str\\n  - gemini_api_key: str  \\n  - unstructured_base_url: str = 'https://transform.unstructured.io'\\n  - gemini_model: str = 'gemini-2.5-flash'\\n  - match_threshold: float = 0.75 (minimum similarity for candidate matching)\\n- Function load_config() that reads from .env and returns Config\\n- Raises clear error if required keys are missing\\n\\n## 6. src/extract/__init__.py (empty)\\n\\n## 7. src/extract/excel_reader.py\\nModule to read Excel files (both shortages and warehouse lists):\\n- Function read_excel(filepath: Path) -> list[dict] that:\\n  - Opens the Excel file with openpyxl\\n  - Auto-detects which sheet has data (skip empty sheets)\\n  - Auto-detects header row (first row with multiple non-empty cells)\\n  - Returns list of dicts with column headers as keys\\n  - Preserves all original values as-is (strings, numbers)\\n  - Handles both Arabic and English column names\\n- Function extract_item_names(rows: list[dict], name_column: str = None) -> list[dict] that:\\n  - If name_column is provided, use it\\n  - Otherwise, auto-detect the column most likely to contain drug names (look for columns with Arabic text, keywords like 'صنف', 'اسم', 'دواء')\\n  - Returns list of {\\\"item_name_raw\\\": str, \\\"source_row\\\": int, \\\"source_file\\\": str}\\n  - Keeps ALL original text including abbreviations, numbers, etc.\\n\\n## 8. src/extract/pdf_reader.py\\nModule to extract drug names from PDF files using Unstructured API:\\n- Function extract_from_pdf(filepath: Path, api_key: str, base_url: str = 'https://transform.unstructured.io') -> dict that:\\n  - Uploads PDF to Unstructured API with profile='best', output='elements'\\n  - Handles polling for async jobs (status checking loop)\\n  - Returns the full JSON response\\n  - Saves the raw response to a .json file alongside the PDF\\n\\n- Function parse_items_from_response(response: dict) -> list[dict] that:\\n  - First checks if 'extracted_data' has items (from Extract step)\\n  - If not, looks for Table elements with text_as_html and parses the HTML tables\\n  - If no structured tables, falls back to parsing the text content\\n  - Returns list of {\\\"item_name_raw\\\": str, \\\"source_page\\\": int|None}\\n\\n- Function extract_items_from_pdf(filepath: Path, api_key: str, base_url: str = 'https://transform.unstructured.io') -> list[dict] that:\\n  - Calls extract_from_pdf to get the response\\n  - Then calls parse_items_from_response\\n  - Adds source_file to each item\\n  - Returns the final list\\n\\nFor the HTML table parsing, use a simple approach:\\n- Parse the text_as_html field from Table elements\\n- Find the column that contains drug names (usually the second column after a code column, or the column with Arabic text)\\n- Extract each row's drug name cell\\n\\nIMPORTANT: The Unstructured API uses:\\n- POST to https://transform.unstructured.io/api/v2/parse\\n- Header: unstructured-api-key\\n- Form data: profile=best, output=elements  \\n- File upload: input=(filename, content, 'application/pdf')\\n- Response may be immediate (200) or async (202 with Location header for polling)\\n- Poll URL returns job status, wait for status='completed'\\n\\n## 9. src/extract/file_handler.py\\nUnified file handler that detects file type and routes to appropriate reader:\\n- Function read_input_files(filepaths: list[Path], role: str, api_key: str = None) -> dict[str, list[dict]] that:\\n  - role is either 'shortages' or 'warehouse'\\n  - For each file, detect if PDF or Excel by extension\\n  - Route to pdf_reader or excel_reader accordingly\\n  - Returns dict mapping filename -> list of extracted items\\n  - Each item has: item_name_raw, source_file, source_page/source_row\\n\\nMake all code clean, with type hints, docstrings, and proper error handling. Use pathlib.Path for all file paths. Print progress messages in Arabic.\",\n    \"inherit\": true,\n    \"model\": \"MODEL_PLACEHOLDER_M26\",\n    \"modelTier\": \"MODEL_TIER_INHERIT\"\n  },\n  \"result\": {\n    \"conversationId\": \"218cbc5d-e25c-452d-99ba-3004c6d3e6f6\",\n    \"logAbsoluteUri\": \"file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/218cbc5d-e25c-452d-99ba-3004c6d3e6f6/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl\",\n    \"workspaceUris\": [\n      \"file:///d%3A/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"spec\": {\n    \"typeName\": \"pharmacy-builder\",\n    \"role\": \"Match and output builder\",\n    \"initialPrompt\": \"Create the following files for the pharmacy drug matching project at d:\\\\AI_Engineer\\\\Pharmacy-agy:\\n\\n## 1. src/match/__init__.py (empty)\\n\\n## 2. src/match/text_match.py\\nText preprocessing and fuzzy matching module:\\n\\n```python\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Text cleaning and fuzzy matching for Arabic drug names.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n```\\n\\nFunctions:\\n- normalize_text(text: str) -> str:\\n  - Convert Arabic-Indic digits (٠-٩) to Western digits (0-9)\\n  - Remove tatweel/kashida (ـ)\\n  - Remove tashkeel/diacritics\\n  - Normalize whitespace (multiple spaces to single)\\n  - Strip leading/trailing whitespace\\n  - Normalize different forms of alef (أ, إ, آ -> ا)\\n  - Normalize taa marbuta (ة -> ه) for search purposes\\n  - DO NOT remove any words, abbreviations, or numbers\\n  - Return normalized text\\n\\n- find_candidates(query: str, items: list[str], threshold: float = 0.60, max_results: int = 5) -> list[tuple[str, float]]:\\n  - Normalize both query and items\\n  - Use rapidfuzz.fuzz.token_sort_ratio for scoring\\n  - Also try rapidfuzz.fuzz.partial_ratio and take the max\\n  - Return top matches above threshold as list of (original_item, score)\\n  - Score is 0-100 from rapidfuzz, we normalize to 0-1\\n\\n- quick_match(query: str, item: str) -> float:\\n  - Quick similarity score between two drug names\\n  - Returns 0.0 to 1.0\\n\\n## 3. src/match/gemini_match.py\\nGemini-based intelligent drug matching:\\n\\n```python\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Use Gemini to resolve ambiguous drug name matches.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n```\\n\\nFunctions:\\n- match_with_gemini(shortage_name: str, candidates: list[dict], api_key: str, model: str = 'gemini-2.5-flash') -> dict:\\n  - Takes a shortage drug name and list of candidate items from a warehouse\\n  - Each candidate has: item_name_raw, source (filename)\\n  - Sends to Gemini with a carefully crafted prompt\\n  - The prompt asks Gemini to:\\n    1. Compare the shortage drug name with each candidate\\n    2. Consider: drug name, concentration/strength, dosage form, pack size\\n    3. Return a JSON with: matched_index (or -1 if no match), confidence (high/medium/low), reason\\n    4. If there's a clear match (same drug, same strength, same form) -> match\\n    5. If drug name matches but strength/form differs -> no match\\n    6. If ambiguous -> return confidence=low\\n  - Uses google.genai client (the new SDK)\\n  - Uses structured output (response_mime_type='application/json')\\n  - Returns: {\\\"matched\\\": bool, \\\"matched_item\\\": str|None, \\\"confidence\\\": str, \\\"reason\\\": str}\\n\\n- batch_match_with_gemini(shortage_items: list[str], warehouse_items: list[str], api_key: str, model: str = 'gemini-2.5-flash') -> list[dict]:\\n  - For efficiency, batch multiple shortage items in one Gemini call\\n  - Send up to 10 shortage items at a time with the full warehouse list\\n  - Ask Gemini to match each shortage item to the best warehouse item\\n  - Returns list of match results\\n\\nThe Gemini prompt should be in Arabic and very specific:\\n- Focus on: اسم الصنف, التركيز, الشكل الدوائي, حجم العبوة\\n- Spelling differences are OK (the same drug with typos)\\n- Different concentrations = different product (NOT a match)\\n- Different forms\n---\nThe checkpoint summary has been truncated due to hitting max length. Please see the conversation log file for the full conversation."}
